※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4632

※ A lambda that brought a variable in by reference reaches the variable where it
※ is, and a variable of the call is gone when the call is.  So it may be called,
※ handed to a call, and bound to a name that does not outlive the variable --
※ and not answered, which would hand back a way of reaching storage that is
※ gone.  It is the rule a reference follows, asked of what a lambda carries.

fn counting(n: u8) → fn(u8) → u8:
    let seen: u8 = n
    λ a: u8 [&seen] → u8 { a + seen }

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    0u6
